  "status": "supplemental-draft-needs-gameplay-review",
  "audit": {
    "scope": "Read-only audit of aligned pointer targets across the original 4194304-byte AMMJ revision 1 ROM. No ROM build or external service was used.",
    "accepted": { "total":96,"shopPriceLabels":70,"villageNames":2,"facePartLabels":1,"battleStatusFormats":2,"rankLabels":20,"explanationOption":1,"outsideExtractorRange":2 },
    "shopEvidence": "The buy/sell table spans 135c2c..135d28 and 135d78..135e74 contain parallel pointers to item-name/price records, separated by 14c bytes. These 35 pairs were excluded by the extractor's kana-density filter because of column-padding spaces. Item names reuse the matching standalone translations from full-01..08. Numeric prices and KANJI:8B currency are unchanged, with the currency retained in column 16.",
    "labelEvidence": "1639db and 1639e5 belong to the same village-name pointer arrays as the adjacent covered names. 163e1b is the eyes entry in the six-part face table 133e64..133e78, between nose and eyebrows. Original proper-name KANJI tokens are preserved.",
    "outsideEvidence": "1680a0 and 1680a7 are the original battle-status format literals referenced at 41e40 and 41e44. HP/MP plus %3d must occupy exactly five columns: an extra separator space wraps the numbers and scrolls away the names. The battle-status scene in tools/original-layout.test.mjs verifies all four original kanji names and HP/MP glyphs and live numeric values at their original positions after a fresh start.",
    "kanjiEvidence": {
      "method": "decodePairs(originalROM, 0x2f9878), 1824 bytes / 57 original 8x8 4bpp tiles. KANJI code 80 is tile 0 (VRAM tile 180); foreground palette index 2. Visually read original bitmaps, not Shift-JIS guesses. Reproduce: node tools/full-inventory.mjs --glyphs 80 88 ab 93 94 83 84 85 86 a5 a6. --validate locks the eight row-bitmask bytes of each inspected tile.",
      "readings": {"80":"桃","88":"下","AB":"旬","93":"初","94":"段","83":"免","84":"許","85":"皆","86":"伝","A5":"説","A6":"明"},
      "rankOwner": "Padded labels: table 133fac has a leading non-rank item at index 0, followed by reviewed words 133fb0..133fd4 inclusive. Literals b404,b428,b4a4,b4f8 point to 133fac; b3e8..b3f6 computes index*4, b4ec loads the selected label into r3 and b4f2 passes it to formatter 3d808. Unpadded labels: literal 3fa6c -> 167f6c, 3fa48..3fa4e indexes (rank-1)*4, 3fa54 calls 3d488. Only ten labels per table are claimed; wider runtime rank validation is not established here.",
      "optionOwner": "167d64 is the choice table base with leading NULL. The three following words 167d68/6c/70 point to yes/no/explanation. Literal 3e0b4 -> 167d64 and 3e088 sets count=3 before 3e08a calls c5b4; branch 3e09a tests result 2. This identifies the third entry as 説明, translated 說明.",
      "bounds": "All 21 additions are NUL-terminated custom strings, complete exact pointerOffsets verified, no format arguments or controls. Twenty rank labels retain the original numeric values, visible widths (2 or 4 columns), and two leading spaces where present. 説明/說明 remain two columns. 免許皆伝 becomes Traditional Chinese 免許皆傳.",
      "twentySecondCandidate": "131411 is 下旬, a suffix of the already-covered festival date at 131407 (full-03, pointer 132250), not an independent menu label. The only exact-target word e8298 is resource data, not a proven renderer pointer. Full-10 preserves sourceHex, translation 下旬, owner and rejected-pointer evidence as excluded-nontext; no write to that word is authorized."
    },
    "baseline": { "alignedPointerTargets": 11759, "tokenValidTargets": 6100, "extractedCandidates": 2592, "extractedReferenced": 2198, "extractedUnreferenced": 394, "catalogOffsetsBeforeSupplement": 2245, "uncoveredNearbyTokenCandidatesBeforeSupplement": 904, "uncoveredDistantHeuristicCandidates": 94 },
    "remaining": [
      "394 no-aligned-pointer candidates are reproducibly classified by --unreferenced: 236 resource fields, 23 covered fragments/misbounded prefixes, 1 diagnostic, 17 readable strings without proven owners, and 117 unresolved short candidates. No computed text owner was proven. Full-10 supplies blocked drafts for the 17 readable strings, not insertion-ready translations.",
      "At this audit snapshot 807 nearby token-valid targets remain outside catalogs. Catalog presence includes exclusions and blocked drafts, so neither that count nor 2396 catalog offsets measures accepted translation coverage. Binary tables, empty fields and unknown targets remain.",
      "The prior 94 distant custom-decoder heuristic candidates include binary resources and Shift-JIS metadata. After full-10 classification, 83 remain outside catalogs; none is accepted merely because it decodes as kana.",
      "Full-10 records all 38 Shift-JIS scan hits: 32 true diagnostic/development-menu strings excluded with source preserved, five player-facing stage-selector labels faithfully translated but blocked pending source-encoding adaptation, and one alternate decoding of covered custom text. Source bytes, table bounds and caller instructions are validated. No Shift-JIS string is submitted to the custom source parser.",
      "All 22 kanji candidates were resolved from original bitmaps: 21 independent labels added here; 131411 is an already-covered 下旬 suffix and excluded as an independent insertion. No kana remains in new translations.",
      "163b50 (%6d plus currency) and 163f5d (%03d : %s) remain unchanged. The latter needs bounded call-site evidence. 163b56 is a currency-only blank field and 163c06 a rule separator, not new Japanese prose.",
      "Yes/no literals 163ee7 and 163eea already belong to menus.zh-Hant.json, with their two aligned pointers each. No additional confident yes/no literal was found.",
      "Unaligned pointers, computed addresses, embedded/relative text, unknown controls, compressed text, title/logo graphics, minigame graphical instructions and other image-only text remain unverified and uncounted. This audit does not establish full-game localization.",
      "No supplemental record has been exercised in its natural gameplay event; final window widths, numeric expansion, font-cache behavior, full tutorials and graphics require emulator review. Other shards retain their independent blocked records and review obligations."
    ]
  },
